    "created_at": "2018-05-22T08:47:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-22T08:47:52Z",
    "body": "> The question is, this is an acceptable data leak?\r\n\r\nIt seems like the data you can infer from the error is fairly narrow: \"This resource had an interesting MIME type.\" Are there cases where that's revealing more than we'd like?\r\n\r\nAlso: if we expand the conditions under which we return a network error (e.g. by making that `From-Origin`'s behavior as well), then we further reduce the granularity of the assumptions an attacker can make.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
